@page "/register"
@using BlazorDLR.Shared.Components

@*
	Web registration - statically rendered, form-posts to /api/v1/auth/web/register (§7.5).
	Same reasoning as /login: the cookie must be set by the endpoint, so the form is not
	inside a running WASM client.

	Registration is what the whole product's "v0.5 signup is not a hurdle" argument buys
	(§7.2), and this page shows the recovery trade-off in plain text next to the empty
	email field. That copy is not marketing; it is what §7.2 requires.
*@

<PageTitle>Register - Dumb Luck Routes</PageTitle>

<div class="page page-standalone page-form form-page">
	<h1>Register</h1>

	<form method="post" action="/api/v1/auth/web/register">
		<label>
			User name - <em>permanent</em>
			<input name="userName" autocomplete="off" required autofocus placeholder="DaveSmith" />
		</label>

		<label>
			Password
			<input name="password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" required />
			<span class="rule-hint">
				At least 6 characters, and at least one uppercase letter,
				one lowercase letter and one digit.
			</span>
		</label>

		<label>
			Email (optional)
			<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
		</label>

		<div class="callout">
			<strong>No email means no recovery and no warning.</strong>
			If you forget your password or lose this device, this account and everything
			in it is gone - a password cannot be reset without an email. An unused account
			holding no saved adventures is deleted after 6 months, and with no email address we
			cannot warn you before it happens. You can add one later.
		</div>

		<button type="submit" class="primary">Create account</button>
	</form>

	<p class="form-note">Already have an account? <a href="/login">Sign in</a>.</p>

	<SourceOfferFooter />
</div>
